---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/common/CodeBlock.astro';
import { FolderTree, ArrowRight, Layers, Box, Cpu, FileCode2 } from 'lucide-preact';

const projectTree = `my_bloom_app/
├── bloom.yaml                  # Unified project configuration & native permissions
├── pubspec.yaml                # Standard Flutter dependencies
├── lib/
│   ├── main.dart               # Framework boot entrypoint (Bloom.boot)
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── app.dart            # Root MaterialApp & theme configuration
│   │   ├── boot.dart           # Dependency injection & service bootstrapper
│   │   ├── guards.dart         # Authentication & route guards
│   │   └── routes.g.dart       # Generated type-safe routing table
│   ├── features/               # Domain-driven feature slices
│   │   ├── auth/
│   │   │   ├── auth_controller.dart
│   │   │   ├── auth_service.dart
│   │   │   └── models/
│   │   └── feed/
│   │       ├── feed_controller.dart
│   │       └── widgets/
│   ├── routes/                 # Next.js-style filesystem routes
│   │   ├── index.dart          # / (Home Route)
│   │   ├── login.dart          # /login
│   │   └── posts/
│   │       ├── index.dart      # /posts
│   │       └── [id].dart       # /posts/:id (Dynamic parameter route)
│   └── bloom_ui/               # Installed shadcn UI primitives (owned by you)
│       ├── primitives/         # Button, Card, Dialog, Sheet, etc.
│       └── theme/              # Design tokens, color schemes, radius scale
└── test/                       # Synchronous unit and widget test suites`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Project Anatomy"
  description="In-depth breakdown of the directory structure and file conventions in a Bloom project."
  currentSlug="getting-started-project-anatomy"
  category="Getting Started"
  toc={[
    { id: 'tree', title: 'Standard Directory Tree' },
    { id: 'lib-app', title: 'The lib/app/ Directory' },
    { id: 'lib-features', title: 'The lib/features/ Directory' },
    { id: 'lib-routes', title: 'The lib/routes/ Directory' },
    { id: 'lib-bloom-ui', title: 'The lib/bloom_ui/ Directory' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div id="overview" class="space-y-4 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-purple-500/10 border border-purple-500/20 text-purple-400 text-xs font-mono font-bold">
        <FolderTree className="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        Conventions
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Project Anatomy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Bloom establishes a clear, domain-driven structure that scales cleanly from solo prototypes to large enterprise applications.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Tree -->
    <section id="tree" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Standard Directory Tree
      </h2>
      <CodeBlock code={projectTree} lang="bash" filename="Project Structure" />
    </section>

    <!-- App Section -->
    <section id="lib-app" class="space-y-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        The lib/app/ Directory
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Contains global application lifecycle configuration:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300 font-mono">
        <li class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-bold">boot.dart</span>: Registers singletons, services, and asynchronous database connections in the DI container.
        </li>
        <li class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-bold">guards.dart</span>: Route interceptors that perform authentication and role-based redirects.
        </li>
        <li class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-bold">routes.g.dart</span>: Generated by the Bloom AST compiler from your <code class="text-slate-400">lib/routes/</code> folder.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Features Section -->
    <section id="lib-features" class="space-y-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        The lib/features/ Directory
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Organizes business logic into vertical domain slices. Each feature encapsulates its own controllers, models, and domain-specific UI widgets.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Routes Section -->
    <section id="lib-routes" class="space-y-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        The lib/routes/ Directory
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        File-based page definitions. Every Dart file represents an accessible URL route, keeping routing decoupled from business logic.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Bloom UI Section -->
    <section id="lib-bloom-ui" class="space-y-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        The lib/bloom_ui/ Directory
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Your local copy of the Bloom UI primitives and design tokens. You own this code and can freely modify styles and behaviors.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Next Page Footer -->
    <div class="pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex justify-between">
      <a
        href="/docs/installation"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold text-xs hover:bg-slate-200 dark:hover:bg-slate-800 transition"
      >
        <span>Previous: Installation</span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/docs/getting-started/bloom-yaml-reference"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-purple-600 text-white font-bold text-xs hover:bg-purple-500 transition shadow-lg"
      >
        <span>Next: bloom.yaml Reference</span>
        <ArrowRight className="w-4 h-4" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
